<title>BELGIUM: SGB declines comment on Accor sale report.</title>
<headline>SGB declines comment on Accor sale report.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian holding company Societe Generale de Belgique SA (SGB), a unit of French Compagnie de Suez, declined to comment on reports from French fund managers that it was selling its eight percent stake in French hotel group Accor at 756 francs per share.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for Accor confirmed the transaction, led by brokerage SBC Warburg.</p>
<p>Earlier this month SGB also declined to comment on similar reports.</p>
<p>-- Geert De Clercq, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6813, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
